The copy is already close to minimal: each `std::vector` copy constructor allocates exactly once and copy-constructs its elements. I can't remove those allocations without changing the object's layout, which the rules forbid. The change below only skips the copy call for an empty `devFields`, which is common. The gain is small, and it is the only change I'm confident is safe without knowing the element types.

```cpp
Mesg::Mesg(const Mesg &mesg)
    : profile(mesg.profile)
    , localNum(mesg.localNum)
    , fields(mesg.fields)
    , devFields()
{
    if (!mesg.devFields.empty())
        devFields = mesg.devFields;
}
```